<title>JAPAN: Aplus expects to get 40 bln yen in help from Sanwa.</title>
<headline>Aplus expects to get 40 bln yen in help from Sanwa.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumer credit company Aplus Co Ltd said on Friday that it expects to receive extra support of about 40 billion yen from Sanwa Bank Ltd.  </p>
<p>The funds will be used to deal with Aplus' problem loans, Aplus said in a statement.</p>
<p>Aplus said it has also decided to withdraw from real estate development in California and will liquidate its U.S. unit Daishinpan Inc.  </p>
<p>Sanwa is Aplus' main creditor bank and owns about five percent of the firm.</p>
</text>
